For each axis, we can find the time interval when the ball is overlapping the brick.
Ball's range on X: `[ball.x0 - r, ball.x0 + r]` to `[ball.x1 - r, ball.x1 + r]`.
Brick's range on X: `[brick.x, brick.x + w]`.

The time `t` when the ball's edge enters the brick on X:
If `vx > 0`, it enters at `t = (brick.x - (ball.x0 + r)) / (vx * dt)`.
If `vx < 0`, it enters at `t = (brick.x + brick.w - (ball.x0 - r)) / (vx * dt)`.

This is the standard AABB vs AABB swept collision (where the ball is treated as a box of size `2r`).

